DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  ttoowwuuppppeerr()  function is the wide‐character equivalent of the ttoouupp‐‐
       ppeerr(3) function.  If _w_c is a lowercase wide character, and there exists
       an uppercase equivalent in the current locale, it returns the uppercase
       equivalent of _w_c.  In all other cases, _w_c is returned unchanged.

       The ttoowwuuppppeerr__ll() function performs the same task, but performs the con‐
       version based on the character type information in the locale specified
       by _l_o_c_a_l_e.  The behavior of ttoowwuuppppeerr__ll() is undefined if _l_o_c_a_l_e is  the
       special  locale  object LLCC__GGLLOOBBAALL__LLOOCCAALLEE (see dduuppllooccaallee(3)) or is not a
       valid locale object handle.

       The argument _w_c must be representable as a _w_c_h_a_r___t and be a valid char‐
       acter in the locale or be the value WWEEOOFF.

